-  deadline is refunded in full; later ones follow the property policy. Cancelling twice is a
-  conflict, never a second refund. Charges and refunds are recorded in a ledger with idempotency
+  deadline is refunded in full; later ones follow the property policy. A non-refundable
+  reservation can still be cancelled, which gives its rooms back, but it refunds nothing at any
+  time, and its cancellation quote says 0 percent. Cancelling twice is a conflict, never a second
+  refund. Charges and refunds are recorded in a ledger with idempotency
   keys.
